  "text": "Zelnick Traders\n\nFacts about lighthouses:\n1. The Pharos of Alexandria, one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World, was built on the island of Pharos in Egypt around 280 BC.\n2. Lighthouses often use Fresnel lenses, which were invented by French physicist Augustin-Jean Fresnel in 1822 to allow light to be seen from much greater distances.\n3. The lighthouse at Dover Castle is the oldest surviving lighthouse in the world, with its origins dating back to the 12th century.\n\nPEXIBI-KATUKA"
